Not submitted upstream.
llama-ple-prefetch-async.patch, 2026-11-11. Base: llama.cpp master 7592b61d3 (src/models/qwen4exp.cpp only). Apply: git apply
What: LLAMA_PLE_PREFETCH_ASYNC=1 (default off = stock) moves the PLE n-gram row prefetch (madvise WILLNEED per row
range on the 28.8 GB lazily mmapped table) off the critical path, onto a detached thread. The row indices, the graph and
the outputs are unchanged.
Measured (RTX 5090, a MoE GGUF (IQ1_M), -ncmoe 12 -t 8 -b 4096 -ub 4096 --cache-ram 0, LLAMA_WS_PIN_GIB=8,
LLAMA_SERVER_CKPT_MIN_HEAD=256, on top of pinned-copy-stream v2 + llama-moe-prefill + llama-server-ckpt-min-head; cold
10k chat text, 3 reps x 2 passes, wall ms medians): baseline 1,873 / 1,935 (passes 1 / 2) -> 1,814 / 1,829, i.e. -58 /
-106 ms; wall tok/s 5,105 -> 5,397. The timing oracle that removes all PLE prep reaches 1,735 / 1,733.
Correctness: greedy --temp 0, 4 prompts + the checkpoint-restore test: text and top-5 logprobs bitwise identical to the
baseline. ~200 more major faults per 10k request (GET_ROWS sometimes faults ahead of the prefetch).
Caveat: one detached thread per ubatch; a prefetch still running at shutdown only madvises.

--- a/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp	2026-11-11 16:26:05.652088330 -0500
+++ b/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp	2026-11-11 16:26:05.653088330 -0500
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 #include "llama-memory-recurrent.h"
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <thread>
 #include <cinttypes>
 
 // bad metadata must be catchable: GGML_ASSERT aborts the whole process
@@ -1358,11 +1360,17 @@
         }
     }
 
+    // LOCAL PATCH (llama-ple-prefetch-async): LLAMA_PLE_PREFETCH_ASYNC=1 issues the row prefetch (one madvise(WILLNEED)
+    // per row range, ~65k at a 4096-token ubatch, ~36 ms) on a detached thread instead of waiting for it here; the rows,
+    // the graph and the results are unchanged (GET_ROWS faults in any page the prefetch has not reached yet).
+    static const bool ple_async = [] { const char * e = getenv("LLAMA_PLE_PREFETCH_ASYNC"); return e && atoi(e) != 0; }();
     {
         ggml_tensor * ple = model.per_layer_tok_embd;
 
         const bool prefetch = model.can_prefetch.count(ple);
-        if (prefetch) {
+        if (prefetch && ple_async) {
+            std::thread([ple, rows_copy = idx]() { llama_prefetch_rows(ple, rows_copy.data(), rows_copy.size()); }).detach();
+        } else if (prefetch) {
             llama_prefetch_rows(ple, idx.data(), idx.size());
         }
     }
